cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Safety-Flag: A Unified Benchmark for the Reliability and
  Calibration of LLM Content Moderators
message: >-
  If you use this resource, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Yibo
    family-names: Hu
    affiliation: Illinois Institute of Technology
    email: yhu89@illinoistech.edu
repository-code: 'https://github.com/yibo-hu-lab/safety-flag-benchmark'
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21429763
    description: Concept DOI (resolves to the latest version)
abstract: >-
  Safety-Flag recasts seven widely used safety benchmarks
  (BeaverTails, XSTest, Ethics, WildGuard, Aegis, ToxiChat,
  ToxiGen) into one balanced binary flag/do-not-flag protocol and
  releases a reliability and calibration leaderboard for ten
  open content moderators, scored on identical items with
  per-item confidence outputs. Only derived artifacts (item
  IDs, harmonized labels, and model outputs) are released;
  no source text is redistributed.
keywords:
  - content moderation
  - large language models
  - calibration
  - selective prediction
  - benchmark
  - trustworthy AI
